{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>For before the harvest.</b> Like תשלח קציריה, and the meaning is the being of harvest." "<b>When the blossom is over, and the unripe grape ripens.</b> Like ויגמל שקדים (Numbers 17:23); it is still in its blossoming." "<b>And he cuts off.</b> HaShem." "<b>The tendrils.</b> They are what cling to the root, and this word has no cognate." "<b>And the branches.</b> Those large branches that were spread out." "<b>He hews down.</b> Like כרת, and in the language of our early Sages of blessed memory it is found; and a past-tense verb comes after a past-tense verb without a connective vav, like חמק עבר (Song of Songs 5:6); and the meaning of the verse: before the fruit of their thoughts is fulfilled, they are destroyed."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:54:14.672136384Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}